+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a value such as `90`, `45s`, or `1h30m` into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A
+bare whole number is a count of seconds. Otherwise the value is one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units
+`d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit can be used at most once, in that order,
+without spaces. Units are case-insensitive, so `1H30M` is the same as `1h30m`. Negative values and decimals are not
+accepted.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout", "1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout", "90"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout", "1.5h"])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.5.1
+```
+
